          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Jean-Jacques Rousseau</strong><br>\nJean-Jacques Rousseau was born on June 28, 1712, in Geneva, Switzerland. He lost his mother just days after his birth, which led to a challenging childhood marked by emotional strain. His father, a watchmaker, had to leave Geneva when Rousseau was ten, leaving him to be raised by an uncle. The hardships of his early years influenced Rousseau's later views on education and society.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rousseau's Education</strong><br>\nDespite his troubled upbringing, Rousseau received a good education in Geneva, which was then a hub for Calvinist thought. His education was informal but comprehensive, including apprenticeships and a brief period of formal schooling. He developed a lifelong love of music and reading, though he frequently moved between jobs and locations as a young man.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Moving to France</strong><br>\nIn his late teens, Rousseau moved to France, where he worked as a secretary and a tutor. This period was significant for his personal development, as he mingled with the French aristocracy and began to question social norms. It was in France that he started to form the philosophical ideas that would later make him famous.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
